  "visibleTextNormalized": "HomeOur communityThe Fortians Union The Fortians Union The Fortian alumni associations began in 1894 to: 1. Build a Strong Community: Create a place where members can connect, have fun, and support each other. 2. Give Back to Fort Street: Actively contribute to the success of Fort Street High School through volunteer work, mentorship, or other initiatives. 3. Celebrate Our Legacy: Honour the rich history and traditions of Fort Street while embracing innovation and progress. For enquiries or to get in touch with the Fortians Union, please contact us via email at: fortians@fortians.au (opens in new window) Faber Est The Fortians Union publishes Faber Est, a regular newsletter. You can explore the latest edition and our growing archive by following this link: Faber Est (opens in new window) . Membership Membership of the Fortians Union is free for the first five years after leaving school. Life membership is available for a one off fee of $50.00. To join, complete the online form by clicking here. (opens in new window) Don't Miss Out Please let us know if your contact details have changed to stay in touch and continue to receive your copy of Faber Est. Update your contact information by clicking here. (opens in new window) Keep in Touch Visit our home page (opens in new window) for the latest updates. Join our Fortians Union Facebook Group (opens in new window) to connect with fellow Fortians. Newsletters Read our latest newsletter and stay connected with our school life. east Events Find out about school events, celebrations and what’s coming up. east Section navigation Our community Alumni The Fortians Union The Fort Street Foundation Foundation Tertiary Bursaries Parents and Citizens Association",
